---
// WHA-130 · sagan.run v1 — single page, static, zero client JS required.
// Extends the approved WHA-131 art-direction frame to sections 01–05.
import '../styles/global.css';
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark" />
<title>Sagan — evidence-based multi-agent orchestration</title>
<meta name="description" content="Extraordinary claims require extraordinary evidence. One accountable PM agent, stateless specialist workers, fresh critics, non-builder verification — APPROVED means verified, not plausible." />
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/Geist-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/Geist-SemiBold.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
<link rel="preload" href="/fonts/GeistMono-Regular.woff2" as="font" type="font/woff2" crossorigin />
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

  <!-- ground index header -->
  <header class="idx">
    <p class="idx-title">01 — Sagan</p>
    <p class="idx-meta">
      <span>Mission documentation · Rev 0</span>
      <button id="gridToggle" type="button" aria-pressed="false" title="Toggle the layout grid (G)">Grid · G</button>
    </p>
  </header>

  <!-- deliberate negative space: the top half belongs to the ground -->
  <div class="void" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  <main>
    <!-- ============ sheet 01 · hero ============ -->
    <section class="sheet" aria-label="01 — Sagan">
      <div class="band">

        <div class="c-1-6">
          <p class="eyebrow">Evidence-based multi-agent orchestration</p>
          <h1>Sagan</h1>
          <p class="tagline">Extraordinary claims require extraordinary evidence.</p>
          <p class="abstract">One accountable PM agent dispatches stateless
            specialist workers — frontend, backend, research — against tickets
            whose acceptance criteria are written before any work starts.
            Nothing user-visible ships without a fresh critic&rsquo;s verdict and a
            non-builder verifier recording commands, exit codes, and screenshots
            at a git SHA. It installs as a self-contained
            <span class="mono">.sagan/</span> directory; humans stay in the loop
            at per-ticket promote gates.</p>
          <p class="stamp">Approved = verified — not plausible</p>
          <div class="ctas">
            <a class="cta" href="https://github.com/thewhatmatters/sagan">&rarr; GitHub repository</a>
            <a class="cta" href="#install">&rarr; Quick-start</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <figure class="c-6-10 div-l">
          <div class="fig-head">
            <span class="t">Evidence records</span>
            <span class="f">jsonl</span>
          </div>
          <div class="panel">
<pre class="ledger" is:raw>{"event":"critique.verdict","ticket":"T-001",
 "round":1,"critic":"critic-claude-fresh",
 "verdict":<b>"NEEDS_EVIDENCE"</b>,"findings":4,
 "artifact_sha":"03f2d22","ts":"2026-08-06"}

{"event":"evidence.recorded","ticket":"T-001",
 "sha":"03f2d2299976eeb269f0452ff111fbbb1e9ca5e4",
 "verifier":"verify-claude",
 "checks":[
   {"ac_ref":"AC5","result":<b>"PASS"</b>,
    "how":"Playwright chromium screenshots at
      375x800 and 1280x900 (light+dark);
      scrollWidth evaluated at 375px",
    "output":"scrollWidth=375 == innerWidth=375
      (light and dark); all sections legible"},
   ⋮  six further checks, AC1–AC7 — all <b>"PASS"</b>
 ],
 "overall":<b>"PASS"</b>,"not_verified":[]}

{"event":"critique.verdict","ticket":"T-001",
 "round":2,"critic":"critic-claude-fresh",
 "verdict":<b>"APPROVED"</b>,"findings":0,
 "artifact_sha":"03f2d22","ts":"2026-08-06"}

{"event":"decision.made","ticket":"T-001",
 "gate":"promote","decision":"promote",
 "by":"randy","ts":"2026-08-06"}</pre>
          </div>
          <figcaption class="caption">Fig. 01 — .sagan/ledger/events.jsonl · ticket T-001, abridged · evidence bound @ 03f2d22</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <div class="c-10-13 div-l">
          <h2 class="clause"><span class="cnum">1.1</span> The rules</h2>
          <ul class="rules">
            <li><strong>AC before dispatch</strong>
              <span>Critic without AC is opinion; critic against AC is a contract.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Flags, never fixes</strong>
              <span>The critic judges; the builder fixes; nobody self-approves.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Builder &ne; verifier</strong>
              <span>Structural, not cultural — the verifier is never the builder.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Reading is not judging</strong>
              <span>NEEDS_EVIDENCE exists so render and runtime claims require execution output.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Approved = verified</strong>
              <span>Ship requires critic approval and non-builder evidence at a git SHA.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Caps are circuit breakers</strong>
              <span>Round limits escalate to a human, never silent approval.</span></li>
            <li><strong>Decisions surface structurally</strong>
              <span>Open decisions arrive as batched questions with recommended defaults — never buried in prose.</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>

      </div>

      <footer class="doc-foot">
        <span>Sagan — Mission documentation · Rev 0</span>
        <span>01</span>
      </footer>
    </section>

    <!-- ground index header, section 02 -->
    <header class="idx idx--sect">
      <p class="idx-title">02 — The Loop</p>
    </header>

    <!-- ============ sheet 02 · the loop ============ -->
    <section class="sheet" aria-label="02 — The Loop">
      <div class="band">

        <div class="c-1-7">
          <p class="eyebrow">Section 02</p>
          <h2>The Loop</h2>

          <h3 class="clause clause--gap"><span class="cnum">2.1</span> The circuit</h3>
          <p class="body">Acceptance criteria are written first. A role-bound
            builder produces the artifact at a digest; a fresh, artifact-only
            critic judges it against the AC. <strong>NEEDS_EVIDENCE</strong>
            routes to a verifier that executes — never the builder — and binds
            evidence to a git SHA. <strong>APPROVED</strong> moves the artifact
            to a human promote gate. Every dispatch, verdict, and evidence
            record lands in the ledger.</p>

          <h3 class="clause clause--gap"><span class="cnum">2.2</span> Verdicts</h3>
          <ul class="verdicts">
            <li><code class="verdict">APPROVED</code>
              <span>Verified, not plausible — critic approval plus non-builder evidence at a git SHA.</span></li>
            <li><code class="verdict">REVISE</code>
              <span>The critic flags; the builder fixes; nobody self-approves.</span></li>
            <li><code class="verdict">NEEDS_EVIDENCE</code>
              <span>Reading is not judging — render and runtime claims require execution output.</span></li>
            <li><code class="verdict">ESCALATE</code>
              <span>Round caps are circuit breakers — limits route to a human, never silent approval.</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <figure class="c-7-13 div-l">
          <div class="fig-head">
            <span class="t">One ticket through the loop</span>
            <span class="f">svg</span>
          </div>
          <div class="panel panel--scroll">
            <svg class="engraving" width="544" height="544" viewBox="-36 0 720 720"
                 role="img" aria-labelledby="fig2t fig2d">
              <title id="fig2t">The Sagan loop, drawn as a thin-line engraving</title>
              <desc id="fig2d">A circular circuit of four stations — ticket plus
                acceptance criteria, build, critique, promote gate — with a
                verify satellite exchanging evidence with critique, a REVISE
                return arc, an ESCALATE ray to a human, and radial lines binding
                every station to the ledger at the center, in the manner of the
                Voyager Golden Record cover.</desc>
              <defs>
                <path id="arw" d="M-9 -3.5 L0 0 L-9 3.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1"/>
              </defs>
              <g fill="none" stroke="currentColor">

                <!-- instrument bezel -->
                <circle cx="310" cy="320" r="252" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="1 11" opacity=".28"/>

                <!-- hub: the ledger, engraved as record grooves -->
                <g stroke-width=".7">
                  <circle cx="310" cy="320" r="38" opacity=".9"/>
                  <circle cx="310" cy="320" r="32" opacity=".75"/>
                  <circle cx="310" cy="320" r="26" opacity=".6"/>
                  <circle cx="310" cy="320" r="20" opacity=".5"/>
                  <circle cx="310" cy="320" r="14" opacity=".4"/>
                  <circle cx="310" cy="320" r="8"  opacity=".35"/>
                </g>
                <line x1="310" y1="320" x2="329" y2="287" stroke-width=".5" opacity=".7"/>
                <circle cx="310" cy="320" r="1.6" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/>
                <!-- hub leader + label -->
                <line x1="252" y1="252" x2="283" y2="293" stroke-width=".4" opacity=".55"/>
                <text x="247" y="244" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" class="soft">.SAGAN/LEDGER/</text>
                <text x="247" y="262" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" class="soft">EVENTS.JSONL</text>

                <!-- radial filings: every station reports to the ledger -->
                <g stroke-width=".6" opacity=".42">
                  <g transform="rotate(0,310,320)"><line x1="310" y1="272" x2="310" y2="146"/></g>
                  <g transform="rotate(90,310,320)"><line x1="310" y1="272" x2="310" y2="146"/></g>
                  <g transform="rotate(180,310,320)"><line x1="310" y1="272" x2="310" y2="184"/></g>
                  <g transform="rotate(270,310,320)"><line x1="310" y1="272" x2="310" y2="146"/></g>
                  <g transform="rotate(145,310,320)"><line x1="310" y1="272" x2="310" y2="160"/></g>
                </g>
                <!-- binary ticks along the filings -->
                <g stroke-width=".8" opacity=".55">
                  <g transform="rotate(0,310,320)">
                    <line x1="305" y1="256" x2="315" y2="256"/><line x1="305" y1="248" x2="315" y2="248"/><line x1="305" y1="232" x2="315" y2="232"/>
                  </g>
                  <g transform="rotate(90,310,320)">
                    <line x1="305" y1="256" x2="315" y2="256"/><line x1="305" y1="240" x2="315" y2="240"/><line x1="305" y1="232" x2="315" y2="232"/><line x1="305" y1="216" x2="315" y2="216"/>
                  </g>
                  <g transform="rotate(180,310,320)">
                    <line x1="305" y1="248" x2="315" y2="248"/><line x1="305" y1="224" x2="315" y2="224"/>
                  </g>
                  <g transform="rotate(270,310,320)">
                    <line x1="305" y1="256" x2="315" y2="256"/><line x1="305" y1="244" x2="315" y2="244"/><line x1="305" y1="236" x2="315" y2="236"/>
                  </g>
                  <g transform="rotate(145,310,320)">
                    <line x1="305" y1="252" x2="315" y2="252"/><line x1="305" y1="244" x2="315" y2="244"/><line x1="305" y1="228" x2="315" y2="228"/><line x1="305" y1="212" x2="315" y2="212"/>
                  </g>
                </g>

                <!-- the ring: AC → BUILD → CRITIQUE → PROMOTE → (shipped) -->
                <g stroke-width="1">
                  <path d="M334.4 121.5 A200 200 0 0 1 508.5 295.6"/>
                  <path d="M508.5 344.4 A200 200 0 0 1 334.4 518.5"/>
                  <path d="M285.6 518.5 A200 200 0 0 1 111.5 344.4"/>
                  <path d="M111.5 295.6 A200 200 0 0 1 285.6 121.5"/>
                </g>
                <use href="#arw" transform="translate(451.4,178.6) rotate(45)"/>
                <use href="#arw" transform="translate(451.4,461.4) rotate(135)"/>
                <use href="#arw" transform="translate(168.6,461.4) rotate(225)"/>
                <use href="#arw" transform="translate(168.6,178.6) rotate(315)"/>
                <text x="466" y="163" font-size="12" class="soft">DISPATCH</text>
                <text x="466" y="486" font-size="12" class="soft">ARTIFACT @ DIGEST</text>
                <text x="154" y="486" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" class="soft">APPROVED</text>
                <text x="154" y="163" text-anchor="end" font-size="12" class="soft">SHIPPED @ SHA</text>

                <!-- REVISE: inner return arc, critique → build -->
                <path d="M330 505 A170 170 0 0 1 495 340" stroke-width=".9" stroke-dasharray="3 5"/>
                <use href="#arw" transform="translate(495,340) rotate(-5)"/>
                <text x="0" y="0" font-size="12" class="soft" text-anchor="middle"
                      transform="translate(368,378) rotate(-45)">REVISE</text>

                <!-- stations -->
                <g stroke-width="1">
                  <circle cx="310" cy="120" r="13"/><circle cx="310" cy="120" r="8.5" stroke-width=".6" opacity=".7"/><circle cx="310" cy="120" r="1.3" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/>
                  <circle cx="510" cy="320" r="13"/><circle cx="510" cy="320" r="8.5" stroke-width=".6" opacity=".7"/><circle cx="510" cy="320" r="1.3" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/>
                  <circle cx="310" cy="520" r="13"/><circle cx="310" cy="520" r="8.5" stroke-width=".6" opacity=".7"/><circle cx="310" cy="520" r="1.3" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/>
                  <circle cx="110" cy="320" r="13"/><circle cx="110" cy="320" r="8.5" stroke-width=".6" opacity=".7"/><circle cx="110" cy="320" r="1.3" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/>
                  <circle cx="505" cy="598" r="13"/><circle cx="505" cy="598" r="8.5" stroke-width=".6" opacity=".7"/><circle cx="505" cy="598" r="1.3" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/>
                </g>
                <text x="310" y="74" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14">TICKET + AC</text>
                <text x="310" y="92" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" class="soft">WRITTEN BEFORE ANY WORK</text>
                <text x="526" y="311" font-size="14">BUILD</text>
                <text x="526" y="330" font-size="13" class="soft">ROLE-BOUND WORKER</text>
                <text x="310" y="478" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14">CRITIQUE</text>
                <text x="310" y="497" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" class="soft">FRESH · ARTIFACT-ONLY</text>
                <text x="88" y="311" text-anchor="end" font-size="14">PROMOTE GATE</text>
                <text x="88" y="330" text-anchor="end" font-size="13" class="soft">HUMAN DECISION</text>
                <text x="505" y="627" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14">VERIFY</text>
                <text x="505" y="646" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" class="soft">EXECUTES · NEVER THE BUILDER</text>

                <!-- critique ⇄ verify: the evidence exchange -->
                <g stroke-width=".9">
                  <line x1="323.4" y1="529.6" x2="488.6" y2="595.8"/>
                  <line x1="491.6" y1="588.4" x2="326.4" y2="522.2"/>
                </g>
                <use href="#arw" transform="translate(488.6,595.8) rotate(21.8) scale(.85)"/>
                <use href="#arw" transform="translate(326.4,522.2) rotate(201.8) scale(.85)"/>
                <text x="0" y="0" font-size="11" class="soft" text-anchor="middle"
                      transform="translate(418,582) rotate(21.8)">NEEDS_EVIDENCE</text>
                <text x="0" y="0" font-size="11" class="soft" text-anchor="middle"
                      transform="translate(398,539) rotate(21.8)">EVIDENCE @ SHA</text>

                <!-- ESCALATE: ray out of the system, to a human -->
                <line x1="293" y1="536" x2="140" y2="625" stroke-width=".9"/>
                <g stroke-width=".8" opacity=".6">
                  <line x1="222" y1="572.5" x2="226" y2="579.5"/>
                  <line x1="206.7" y1="581.5" x2="210.7" y2="588.5"/>
                  <line x1="191.5" y1="590.5" x2="195.5" y2="597.5"/>
                </g>
                <rect x="128" y="625" width="12" height="12" stroke-width="1"/>
                <text x="134" y="657" text-anchor="middle" font-size="14">ESCALATE</text>
                <text x="134" y="676" text-anchor="middle" font-size="13" class="soft">ROUND CAPS &rarr; A HUMAN</text>

              </g>
            </svg>
          </div>
          <figcaption class="caption">Fig. 02 — the loop, engraved · every station files to the ledger at center · after the Voyager Golden Record</figcaption>
        </figure>

      </div>

      <footer class="doc-foot">
        <span>Sagan — Mission documentation · Rev 0</span>
        <span>02</span>
      </footer>
    </section>

    <!-- ground index header, section 03 -->
    <header class="idx idx--sect">
      <p class="idx-title">03 — The Rules</p>
    </header>

    <!-- ============ sheet 03 · the rules as clauses ============ -->
    <section class="sheet" aria-label="03 — The Rules">
      <div class="band">
        <div class="c-1-7">
          <p class="eyebrow">Section 03</p>
          <h2>The Rules</h2>
          <p class="body">Seven clauses, each enforced structurally rather than
            by good intentions — and each with a receipt in the ledger of this
            repo&rsquo;s own first run. Verdicts:
            <span class="mono">APPROVED&thinsp;|&thinsp;REVISE&thinsp;|&thinsp;NEEDS_EVIDENCE&thinsp;|&thinsp;ESCALATE</span>.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="band" style="margin-top:48px;">
        <div class="c-1-13">
          <div class="rt-head band">
            <span class="c-1-4">Clause</span>
            <span class="c-4-9">Meaning</span>
            <span class="c-10-13">Receipt — ledger, T-001 run</span>
          </div>
          <ul class="rt">
            <li class="band">
              <h3 class="rt-name c-1-4"><span class="cnum">3.1</span> AC before dispatch</h3>
              <p class="rt-mean c-4-9">Critic without AC is opinion; critic against
                AC is a contract. No work is dispatched before the ticket&rsquo;s
                acceptance-criteria block is written.</p>
              <p class="rt-ref c-10-13 div-l"><span class="rlabel">Receipt</span>
                tickets/T-001.md · AC committed before dispatch · sagan.yaml
                <b>ac_before_dispatch: required</b></p>
            </li>
            <li class="band">
              <h3 class="rt-name c-1-4"><span class="cnum">3.2</span> Flags, never fixes</h3>
              <p class="rt-mean c-4-9">The critic judges; the builder fixes; nobody
                self-approves. Findings route back to the builder — the critic
                never patches the artifact.</p>
              <p class="rt-ref c-10-13 div-l"><span class="rlabel">Receipt</span>
                critique.verdict · round 1 · <b>"findings":4</b> — flagged to the
                builder, fixed by the builder</p>
            </li>
            <li class="band">
              <h3 class="rt-name c-1-4"><span class="cnum">3.3</span> Builder &ne; verifier</h3>
              <p class="rt-mean c-4-9">Structural, not cultural — the verifier is
                never the builder, so evidence cannot be produced by the party
                whose work it certifies.</p>
              <p class="rt-ref c-10-13 div-l"><span class="rlabel">Receipt</span>
                builder <b>"frontend-claude-subagent"</b> &ne; verifier
                <b>"verify-claude"</b></p>
            </li>
            <li class="band">
              <h3 class="rt-name c-1-4"><span class="cnum">3.4</span> Reading is not judging</h3>
              <p class="rt-mean c-4-9"><strong>NEEDS_EVIDENCE</strong> exists so
                render and runtime claims require execution output — a critic
                cannot approve a layout from source code.</p>
              <p class="rt-ref c-10-13 div-l"><span class="rlabel">Receipt</span>
                round 1 <b>"NEEDS_EVIDENCE"</b> — 375px legibility and dark
                rendering refused on a read</p>
            </li>
            <li class="band">
              <h3 class="rt-name c-1-4"><span class="cnum">3.5</span> Approved = verified</h3>
              <p class="rt-mean c-4-9">Ship requires critic approval
                <strong>and</strong> non-builder evidence at a git SHA — approval
                on plausibility alone does not exist.</p>
              <p class="rt-ref c-10-13 div-l"><span class="rlabel">Receipt</span>
                evidence.recorded @ <b>03f2d22</b> · 7/7 checks <b>"PASS"</b> ·
                then round 2 <b>"APPROVED"</b></p>
            </li>
            <li class="band">
              <h3 class="rt-name c-1-4"><span class="cnum">3.6</span> Caps are circuit breakers</h3>
              <p class="rt-mean c-4-9">Round limits escalate to a human, never to
                silent approval. Repeated identical failures escalate too — the
                strategy may be wrong.</p>
              <p class="rt-ref c-10-13 div-l"><span class="rlabel">Receipt</span>
                sagan.yaml · max_rounds <b>correctness: 5, quality: 3</b> ·
                on_cap <b>ESCALATE</b></p>
            </li>
            <li class="band">
              <h3 class="rt-name c-1-4"><span class="cnum">3.7</span> Decisions surface structurally</h3>
              <p class="rt-mean c-4-9">Open decisions arrive as batched questions
                with recommended defaults — never buried in prose, never
                one-at-a-time when they can batch.</p>
              <p class="rt-ref c-10-13 div-l"><span class="rlabel">Receipt</span>
                decision.needed &rarr; decision.made · gate <b>"promote"</b> ·
                by <b>"randy"</b></p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <footer class="doc-foot">
        <span>Sagan — Mission documentation · Rev 0</span>
        <span>03</span>
      </footer>
    </section>

    <!-- ground index header, section 04 -->
    <header class="idx idx--sect">
      <p class="idx-title">04 — The Receipts</p>
    </header>

    <!-- ============ sheet 04 · the worked example ============ -->
    <section class="sheet" aria-label="04 — The Receipts">
      <div class="band">

        <div class="c-1-6">
          <p class="eyebrow">Section 04</p>
          <h2>The Receipts</h2>

          <h3 class="clause clause--gap"><span class="cnum">4.1</span> Worked example — T-001</h3>
          <p class="body">This repo ran its own first ticket, and the whole trail
            is committed. The critic refused to approve 375px legibility and
            dark-mode rendering from reading source; verify executed instead,
            and bound the evidence to commit
            <strong class="mono">03f2d22</strong>.</p>
          <ol class="trail">
            <li><code class="verdict">DISPATCH</code>
              <span>Frontend lane · role-bound builder <b>frontend-claude-subagent</b>, context pack of pointers.</span></li>
            <li><code class="verdict">BUILD</code>
              <span><b>src/index.html</b> at a digest · two ambiguities flagged on the ticket, not guessed silently.</span></li>
            <li><code class="verdict">CRITIQUE · R1</code>
              <span>Fresh critic, artifact-only isolation: <b>NEEDS_EVIDENCE</b>, 4 findings.</span></li>
            <li><code class="verdict">VERIFY</code>
              <span>Never the builder. Playwright screenshots at 375&times;800 and 1280&times;900, both schemes; measured <b>scrollWidth 375 = innerWidth 375</b>; 7/7 AC checks <b>PASS</b>, bound @ <b>03f2d22</b>.</span></li>
            <li><code class="verdict">CRITIQUE · R2</code>
              <span>Second fresh critic, artifact plus evidence: <b>APPROVED</b>, zero findings.</span></li>
            <li><code class="verdict">PROMOTE</code>
              <span>Human decision at the gate · <b>by: randy</b>.</span></li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <figure class="c-6-13 div-l">
          <div class="fig-head">
            <span class="t">The committed evidence</span>
            <span class="f">png · @ 03f2d22</span>
          </div>
          <div class="ev-grid">
            <figure class="ev">
              <img src="/evidence/t-001/1280-light.png" width="1280" height="900" loading="lazy"
                   alt="Verify's screenshot of the T-001 page at 1280 by 900, light scheme: an Agent Fleet header, the heading 'A minimal test bed for contract-driven agent orchestration', a status pill reading 'v0 test run · T-001', three feature cards — Dispatch, Critique, Evidence — side by side, and a footer with the repo path." />
